  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Show that the line passing through $A(1,6)$ and $B(2,7)$ is parallel to the line passing through $X(-1,6)$ and $Y(2,9)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both gradients are $1$, so $AB\\parallel XY$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{7-6}{2-1}\\\\m_{AB}&=1\\\\m_{XY}&=\\frac{9-6}{2-(-1)}\\\\m_{XY}&=\\frac{3}{3}\\\\m_{XY}&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe two lines have the same gradient, so $AB\\parallel XY$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
